;; Go's read level's divergences (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, REAP1, RPS3): the classes of the
;; non-passes of repr/go's native reader against the helper (bin/repr-go native-check, 22 corpora;
;; its numbers in test/repr/go/native-check-results.edn, bin/reap record-native-check), in
;; test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A case is "RESULT CORPUS: why": "raw-only CORPUS: the final
;; conversion's failure" (a dump with raw forms only), "extra CORPUS: the helper's failure" (dumped
;; natively, not by the helper), "rejected CORPUS: N files go/parser rejects", and a key of
;; test/repr/go/native-known.edn "known KEY: reason". Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :invalid-programs
  :title "invalid programs the converter cannot convert (raw forms only)"
  :kind :design
  :why "the forms are for valid Go: $GOROOT/test's errorcheck programs invalid in a way the final conversion cannot represent have raw forms only (judged on them by goi, GPS9)"
  :decided "GC47 (a); doc/go/GO-PARSER-SURVEY.md, GPS9, \"As built: GP3\""
  :match [#"^raw-only linux-errtest: "]}
 {:id :goos-other-boards
  :title "TamaGo's goos packages for other boards and architectures"
  :kind :design
  :why "packages of the goos module that do not type-check for the corpus's architecture (other boards and SoCs): the helper dumps them with type errors and the final conversion stops, or the helper cannot dump them at all (another architecture's assembly, undefined names); their raw forms are read"
  :decided "doc/go/GO-PARSER-SURVEY.md, \"As built: GP3\", GPS17"
  :match [#"^raw-only goos-(amd64|arm64): " #"^extra goos-(amd64|arm64): "]}
 {:id :parser-rejects
  :title "files go/parser rejects"
  :kind :design
  :why "no tree to compare: rejected by both readers, judged on gc's syntax errors (gc's syntax run by goi)"
  :decided "doc/go/GO-PARSER-SURVEY.md, GPS9, \"As built: GP6\""
  :match [#"^rejected linux-errtest: "]}
]
